\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1\lang1033\f1\fs40\b Travel Companion V1\par
\f0\fs24\b0 CEO Pitch Document\par
\par
\b Executive Summary\par
\b0 Travel Companion V1 is a functional, production-ready foundation for group trip expense management. Users can create trips, add members, record expenses, split costs, and view settlement outcomes instantly.\par
V1 solves the core trust problem in shared spending: everyone can see exactly who paid, who consumed, and who owes whom.\par
\par
\b Problem We Are Solving\par
\b0 Group travel spending is usually tracked in chats or spreadsheets, creating confusion, delayed settlements, and social friction. V1 provides a single source of truth with transparent calculations and clear final settlement lines.\par
\par
\b What We Shipped in V1\par
\b0 1. Trip lifecycle: create and manage trips.\par
2. Member management: add participants quickly.\par
3. Expense capture: log payer, amount, date, and split participants.\par
4. Equal split engine: deterministic split calculations with rounding safety.\par
5. Balance engine: paid/share/net computation per member.\par
6. Settlement engine: optimized debtor-to-creditor settlement outputs.\par
7. Day-wise + overall summaries for better spend visibility.\par
8. Expense edit/delete support for correction workflows.\par
\par
\b Business Value\par
\b0 - Faster trip settlement cycles.\par
- Higher user trust via transparent and reproducible math.\par
- Lower conflict in group finances through clear accountability.\par
- Strong platform base for monetizable premium capabilities in V2/V3.\par
\par
\b Product Experience Highlights\par
\b0 - Minimal, clean UI focused on speed of entry.\par
- Bright visual design with clear hierarchy.\par
- Form validation to reduce bad inputs.\par
- Immediate data refresh after create/update/delete actions.\par
\par
\b Technical Architecture\par
\b0 - Frontend: Next.js App Router + TypeScript (strict mode).\par
- Backend: Supabase PostgreSQL.\par
- Validation + forms: zod + react-hook-form.\par
- Layered design: UI \u8594{} Services \u8594{} Supabase client \u8594{} DB.\par
- All DB queries are isolated in service layer to keep UI clean and maintainable.\par
\par
\b Data Model (Core)\par
\b0 - trips\par
- members (trip-scoped)\par
- expenses (trip-scoped, payer, amount, date)\par
- expense_splits (member-level owed rows)\par
\par
\b Quality and Reliability\par
\b0 - Split math tests are implemented and passing.\par
- Build, lint, and runtime flows are validated.\par
- Migration + seed scripts available for reproducible setup.\par
\par
\b Key Decision in V1\par
\b0 Settlement follows net accounting:\par
Net = Paid - Share\par
Then debtors pay creditors until all nets reach zero.\par
This mirrors expected behavior in mature split apps and scales cleanly with complex trips.\par
\par
\b Risks / Known Constraints\par
\b0 - No authentication or role-based access control in V1.\par
- Equal-split-first model; advanced split modes are future scope.\par
- No receipts/OCR and no notifications yet.\par
\par
\b V2 Recommendations\par
\b0 1. Authentication + trip access controls.\par
2. Advanced splits (percent, exact amount, unequal shares).\par
3. Personal expense toggle and richer split presets.\par
4. Analytics layer: who paid most, spend by day/category.\par
5. Export/share settlement summary (PDF/WhatsApp-ready).\par
\par
\b V3 Direction\par
\b0 - Real-time collaboration.\par
- Multi-currency support with conversion history.\par
- Receipt capture, OCR, and automated categorization.\par
- Team/organization travel workspace.\par
\par
\b Ask from CEO\par
\b0 Approve progression from V1 to V2 with focus on authentication, advanced split options, and shareable settlement outputs. These three additions materially improve trust, retention, and monetization readiness.\par
\par
\b Conclusion\par
\b0 V1 has successfully de-risked the core product thesis: users can record shared trip expenses and settle transparently with minimal friction. The foundation is stable, extensible, and ready for growth-stage feature investment.\par
